===Etymology 1===
{{suffix|en|sleep|er}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[sleep]]s.
#: {{ux|en|I'm a light '''sleeper''': I get woken up by the smallest of sounds.}}
#: {{ux|en|She's a heavy '''sleeper''': it takes a lot to wake her up.}}
# That which lies [[dormant]], as a [[law]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Of Judicature}}
#*: Therefore let penal laws, if they have been '''sleepers''' of long, or if they be grown unfit for the present time, be by wise judged confined in the execution {{...}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1958|author=Duncan Leroy Kennedy|title=Bill drafting|page=12|text=The object of these provisions is to prevent insertion of "jokers" or "'''sleepers'''" in bills and securing passage under the false color of the title.}}
# A [[spy]], [[saboteur]], or [[terrorist]] who lives [[unobtrusively]] in a [[community]] until [[activated]] by a [[prearranged]] [[signal]]; may be part of a [[sleeper cell]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1969|author=United States Congress|title=Departments of Treasury and Post Office and Executive Office Appropriations for 1970: Hearings|section=(91st Congress, First Session, parts 2-3)|page=479|text=We are up against the pros; and pros who have been involved in this kind of activity for many years. {{...}} The public apathy today is disturbing — few realize, Mr. Chairman, that there are '''sleepers''' in this country and we know that they are able to manipulate at will behind the scenes.}}
# A small [[starter]] [[earring]], worn to prevent a piercing from closing.
# A [[railway]] [[sleeping car]].
#: {{ux|en|We spent a night on an uncomfortable '''sleeper''' between Athens and Vienna.}}
# {{lb|en|martial arts|wrestling}} A [[sleeper hold]].
# Something that [[achieve]]s [[unexpected]] [[success]] after an [[interval]] of time.
#: {{syn|en|sleeper hit}}
#: {{ux|en|A box-office bomb when it first came out, the film was a '''sleeper''', becoming much more popular decades after being released.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=Marvin B. Scott|title=The Racing Game|page=160|text=For example, the [racehorse] trainer may have tipped a betting syndicate that he is about to unleash a '''sleeper''' {{...}}}}
# A [[goby]]-like bottom-feeding freshwater fish of the family {{taxlink|Odontobutidae|family|ver=161011}}.
# A [[nurse shark]] (family {{taxlink|Ginglymostomatidae|family|ver=161011}}).
# A type of [[pajamas|pajama]] for a person, especially a child, that covers the whole body, including the feet.
#: {{ux|en|Aaron, Devin, and Laura looked so comfy in their '''sleepers'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} An automobile which has been internally modified to excess, while retaining a mostly stock appearance in order to fool opponents in a drag race, or to avoid the attention of the police.
#: {{ant|en|cop magnet|rice burner|racecar}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[sedative]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1995|artist={{w|Faithless}}|album=Reverence|title=Insomnia|passage=At least a couple of weeks since I last slept, / Kept takin' '''sleepers''', but now I keep myself pepped.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|gambling}} A [[bet]] placed on the gambling table and then forgotten about by the gambler.

